<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    The same as `values-v31/styles.xml`, and this copy is load-bearing.

    Android resolves qualifiers in a fixed order of precedence, and **night mode
    outranks platform version**. So on an Android 13 phone with the system in
    dark mode, `values-night/styles.xml` wins over `values-v31/styles.xml` — and
    that file says nothing about the splash screen, so the system falls back to
    its own: the application icon, `@mipmap/ic_launcher`, on a plain background,
    which is the whole of **ISSUE 24**'s "glimpses of the old app icon".

    Duplicating four lines is the price of that rule. The alternative — one file
    that varies — does not exist, because there is no qualifier for "31 or above,
    regardless of night".

    The values are identical to the day file on purpose, not by oversight. The
    reasoning is written out there and in `values/colors.xml`: the app defaults
    to dark whatever the phone is set to, so the launch window is dark in both.
-->
<resources>
    <style name="LaunchTheme" parent="@android:style/Theme.Black.NoTitleBar">
        <item name="android:windowBackground">@drawable/launch_background</item>
        <item name="android:windowSplashScreenBackground">@color/lamplight_canvas</item>
        <item name="android:windowSplashScreenAnimatedIcon">@mipmap/ic_launcher_foreground</item>
    </style>

    <style name="NormalTheme" parent="@android:style/Theme.Black.NoTitleBar">
        <item name="android:windowBackground">?android:colorBackground</item>
    </style>
</resources>
